1
00:00:02,110 --> 00:00:06,430
There are strange phenomenon
in this world

2
00:00:06,430 --> 00:00:09,800
that science is unable to explain.

3
00:00:10,110 --> 00:00:12,680
When people came
face to face with them,

4
00:00:12,760 --> 00:00:17,640
all they can do is tremble
upon the terror of the darkness.

5
00:00:18,200 --> 00:00:22,410
But there are those who fight every day
to shine a ray of hope

6
00:00:22,410 --> 00:00:25,400
into that chaotic darkness.

7
00:00:25,570 --> 00:00:27,790
People call them...

8
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:30,350
Psychics.

9
00:00:35,450 --> 00:00:37,160
(MOB MOB WOW!)

10
00:00:38,260 --> 00:00:40,040
(MOB MOB WOW!)

11
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:42,860
(MOB MOB WOW!)

12
00:00:44,010 --> 00:00:45,680
(MOB MOB WOW!)

13
00:00:47,100 --> 00:00:49,840
I realized that our youth is Grey

14
00:00:49,840 --> 00:00:52,730
The origin of this uneasiness
Is yet unknown

15
00:00:52,810 --> 00:00:55,240
Trains of emotions keep running
Through my brain

16
00:00:55,240 --> 00:00:58,410
Struggling through this adolescence

17
00:00:58,540 --> 00:01:01,370
Don't disturb my deep psyche

18
00:01:01,370 --> 00:01:04,040
Who is that behind you?

19
00:01:04,170 --> 00:01:07,830
Opposing ideas creates distortion

20
00:01:07,830 --> 00:01:11,250
Exorcise all the sorrow

21
00:01:11,420 --> 00:01:14,940
So, do what you can now

22
00:01:15,010 --> 00:01:16,860
My life

23
00:01:17,090 --> 00:01:20,970
Finally, break it down

24
00:01:22,460 --> 00:01:25,310
(Want) Both greed
(Young) And honesty

25
00:01:25,310 --> 00:01:28,190
(Burn) Are growing
(1) On this chest of mine

26
00:01:28,190 --> 00:01:30,960
(Trance) I'm not waking up
(Chance) I want to wake up

27
00:01:30,960 --> 00:01:33,900
(Stance) These two different faces of mine
(1) Are standing back-to-back

28
00:01:33,900 --> 00:01:36,400
Taking things as it is

29
00:01:36,400 --> 00:01:39,840
In this free relation
where we resent each other

30
00:01:39,930 --> 00:01:42,120
Once these two become one

31
00:01:42,120 --> 00:01:44,120
That smile becomes one

32
00:01:44,120 --> 00:01:47,220
And only "1"
(MOB MOB WOW!)

33
00:01:47,870 --> 00:01:50,880
"1"
(MOB MOB WOW!)

34
00:01:51,230 --> 00:01:52,280
(MOB MOB WOW!)

35
00:01:52,280 --> 00:01:55,190
One and only "1"
(MOB MOB WOW!)

36
00:01:55,340 --> 00:01:56,890
"1"

37
00:01:56,890 --> 00:01:58,050
(MOB MOB WOW!)

38
00:01:58,050 --> 00:02:00,340
One and only "1"

39
00:02:02,750 --> 00:02:04,870
Future aspirations form?

40
00:02:04,950 --> 00:02:07,720
What, you haven't finished writing yours?

41
00:02:07,810 --> 00:02:10,690
Yeah, I couldn't think of one...

42
00:02:10,860 --> 00:02:14,690
I'm going to a university that
has a subject regarding UFOs.

43
00:02:14,890 --> 00:02:17,280
I'll probably try
to get a work on a game company.

44
00:02:17,350 --> 00:02:19,410
I just wrote office worker.

45
00:02:19,620 --> 00:02:22,730
I'm still a first-year,
so I'm still thinking about it.

46
00:02:22,830 --> 00:02:24,370
I see.

47
00:02:24,810 --> 00:02:27,580
But all of you really
thought well about it.

48
00:02:29,370 --> 00:02:33,820
By the way, apparently Takane
got accepted to Citrus Chilli High.

49
00:02:33,930 --> 00:02:36,020
Citrus Chilli High? Isn't that...

50
00:02:36,260 --> 00:02:39,770
Yeah, the one you need a deviation
score above 65 to enter.

51
00:02:39,770 --> 00:02:42,570
One of the top three high-level
schools in the prefecture.

52
00:02:44,400 --> 00:02:49,390
Well, she has a really good head
on her shoulders, unlike us.

53
00:02:50,220 --> 00:02:52,910
Tsubomi is so amazing...

54
00:02:53,200 --> 00:02:55,280
Wait, is that for real?

55
00:02:55,380 --> 00:02:59,480
Citrus High has a joint business
with a high school in England,

56
00:02:59,480 --> 00:03:01,530
so apparently you can get
to study abroad there.

57
00:03:01,800 --> 00:03:04,490
Studying abroad sounds really nice.

58
00:03:06,910 --> 00:03:09,910
(Progress until Mob explodes: 7%)

59
00:03:09,910 --> 00:03:11,100
(Spirits and Such Consultation Office)

60
00:03:11,210 --> 00:03:15,130
Right, I filled one of these
back at high school, too.

61
00:03:15,310 --> 00:03:17,750
Well, good thing for you,

62
00:03:17,850 --> 00:03:20,880
you already secured
your future workplace.

63
00:03:21,070 --> 00:03:21,840
Huh?

64
00:03:21,840 --> 00:03:23,890
This place, of course.

65
00:03:23,970 --> 00:03:26,380
This job is your calling, isn't it?

66
00:03:27,290 --> 00:03:30,100
Isn't this just a part-time job?

67
00:03:30,330 --> 00:03:32,380
Now then, who knows?

68
00:03:32,590 --> 00:03:35,450
In the future, there's a possibility
this will become a full-fledged

69
00:03:35,450 --> 00:03:38,150
that hires multiple full-time
employees, you know?

70
00:03:38,910 --> 00:03:40,650
Future, huh?

71
00:03:41,790 --> 00:03:46,750
Have you already thought about making
a consultation office back in middle school?

72
00:03:46,850 --> 00:03:48,910
What? Of course not.

73
00:03:49,050 --> 00:03:51,150
What kind of middle schooler
would think of that?

74
00:03:51,250 --> 00:03:53,640
So why did you end up doing it?

75
00:03:53,640 --> 00:03:54,670
Huh?!

76
00:03:54,670 --> 00:03:58,480
Why? Well, you see, one day...

77
00:03:58,600 --> 00:04:03,370
I just realised that I have
a rare special ability.

78
00:04:03,440 --> 00:04:07,230
It just also happens that I already
too good at my job at the time,

79
00:04:07,230 --> 00:04:10,880
so I decided to challenge myself
with new things instead.

80
00:04:11,060 --> 00:04:15,220
You did great at your job,
and then opened your own office.

81
00:04:15,520 --> 00:04:17,690
You really are amazing, Master.

82
00:04:17,760 --> 00:04:18,840
You could say that.

83
00:04:18,920 --> 00:04:21,890
-I finished cleaning the toilet.
-Okay.

84
00:04:22,410 --> 00:04:25,930
Hey, you don't have to report
every single thing you do, you know?

85
00:04:26,030 --> 00:04:27,660
Y-yes, Sir.

86
00:04:27,750 --> 00:04:30,020
Good day to you, Shigeo.

87
00:04:30,120 --> 00:04:31,710
Uh, yeah...

88
00:04:31,960 --> 00:04:34,300
We're going to have a client here soon.

89
00:04:34,410 --> 00:04:35,830
Listen up, Serizawa!

90
00:04:36,430 --> 00:04:41,280
You may already be formally hired here,
but you're still just a fresh newbie!

91
00:04:41,400 --> 00:04:46,210
Make sure you watch closely how I handle
the customers and learn the basics.

92
00:04:46,420 --> 00:04:48,270
Yes, Sir! I will do my best.

93
00:04:48,370 --> 00:04:51,490
Serizawa is older than
Master Reigen, and yet...

94
00:04:54,110 --> 00:04:57,740
I found this ornament at
an antique shop on my travel.

95
00:04:57,740 --> 00:05:03,120
Now that I think about it, bad things
started happening ever since I got it.

96
00:05:03,120 --> 00:05:05,110
I couldn't sleep properly.

97
00:05:05,590 --> 00:05:08,820
People also said that
my complexion is looking worse.

98
00:05:09,040 --> 00:05:11,580
Can you please see
if there's anything wrong with it?

99
00:05:11,730 --> 00:05:13,520
Very well.

100
00:05:18,440 --> 00:05:21,040
By the way, how much
did you buy it for?

101
00:05:21,120 --> 00:05:22,550
I bought it for 80,000 yen.

102
00:05:22,760 --> 00:05:23,770
So expensive.

103
00:05:23,770 --> 00:05:25,320
So expensive...

104
00:05:25,780 --> 00:05:29,550
As far as I checked,
I don't sense anything spiritual...

105
00:05:29,550 --> 00:05:30,650
Master.

106
00:05:30,730 --> 00:05:32,210
What is it, Mob?

107
00:05:32,320 --> 00:05:35,840
I suggest you don't touch
that ornament any further.

108
00:05:35,970 --> 00:05:36,840
Huh?

109
00:05:36,970 --> 00:05:38,930
There's something like a grudge in it.

110
00:05:38,930 --> 00:05:42,110
Tons of bad things are swirling in it.

111
00:05:42,480 --> 00:05:47,150
I think it would be pretty dangerous
if we let it be.

112
00:05:48,980 --> 00:05:51,400
On second thought,
we'll exorcise it.

113
00:05:51,400 --> 00:05:54,580
Would you wait at the cafe
above this floor for a moment?

114
00:05:54,700 --> 00:05:57,210
(Spirits and Such Consultation Office)
O-okay...

115
00:05:57,480 --> 00:06:00,590
-Your opinion is duly noted, Mob.
-Yes?

116
00:06:00,590 --> 00:06:03,640
So, Serizawa, what about you?

117
00:06:03,720 --> 00:06:05,200
Me?

118
00:06:05,250 --> 00:06:12,490
All I can see is that
it's a pretty wicked cursed ornament...

119
00:06:12,920 --> 00:06:14,510
Look here, Serizawa.

120
00:06:14,760 --> 00:06:17,890
Why are you just spacing around
without saying anything?

121
00:06:18,350 --> 00:06:21,800
Let's say that if I "actually"
didn't realize it was cursed,

122
00:06:21,800 --> 00:06:23,450
won't it be a big problem?

123
00:06:23,550 --> 00:06:25,550
Huh? Uh...

124
00:06:25,790 --> 00:06:30,490
All this was a test of whether
you'll notice my mistake or not.

125
00:06:30,750 --> 00:06:31,960
Wha...?!

126
00:06:32,020 --> 00:06:34,260
T-then, did I...?

127
00:06:34,350 --> 00:06:37,950
Well, you're a newbie here,
so I'll go easy on you.

128
00:06:38,130 --> 00:06:41,050
How about you try redeeming yourself?

129
00:06:41,130 --> 00:06:44,190
-Try exorcising it on your own.
-Y-yes, Sir!

130
00:07:02,750 --> 00:07:04,340
I did it.

131
00:07:04,660 --> 00:07:05,910
How did it go, Mob?

132
00:07:05,910 --> 00:07:08,570
Serizawa is really powerful.

133
00:07:08,860 --> 00:07:09,740
All right!

134
00:07:09,740 --> 00:07:13,760
Good job, Serizawa.
Keep up the good work.

135
00:07:16,430 --> 00:07:18,400
That was from the impact just now...

136
00:07:18,530 --> 00:07:22,460
I-it's my fault...!
I damaged this 80,000 yen ornament...!

137
00:07:22,840 --> 00:07:24,960
I'll go get a loan!

138
00:07:24,960 --> 00:07:26,000
Hold it!

139
00:07:26,120 --> 00:07:27,420
Don't worry.

140
00:07:27,760 --> 00:07:30,130
I'll do something about it.

141
00:07:30,210 --> 00:07:32,970
W-what are you going to do...?

142
00:07:36,440 --> 00:07:39,450
Rice Grain Big Bang!

143
00:07:42,020 --> 00:07:45,840
A technique where Reigen unleashes
the maximum potential of a rice grain.

144
00:07:45,840 --> 00:07:48,360
One of Reigen's many special technique.

145
00:07:50,230 --> 00:07:53,540
I-it's fixed!

146
00:07:53,770 --> 00:07:59,340
At this moment, Serizawa is impressed
by Reigen's limitless abilities

147
00:07:59,340 --> 00:08:02,040
and learned for the first time
just how wide the world is.

148
00:08:03,160 --> 00:08:05,430
What's wrong, Shige?

149
00:08:05,550 --> 00:08:07,770
You're not moving your chopsticks.

150
00:08:07,960 --> 00:08:11,310
I have to write down
my future aspirations,

151
00:08:11,380 --> 00:08:13,130
but I have no idea what to write.

152
00:08:13,330 --> 00:08:16,730
You still have like nearly 10 years
until you graduate from university,

153
00:08:16,730 --> 00:08:19,340
so why not just write
office worker for now?

154
00:08:19,410 --> 00:08:22,480
Come on, you're being too
simple-minded here.

155
00:08:22,620 --> 00:08:26,590
I still haven't decided
which high school I'll attend either.

156
00:08:26,940 --> 00:08:29,130
If you haven't found out
what you want to do,

157
00:08:29,130 --> 00:08:33,110
then how about making a living
doing the things you're good at?

158
00:08:33,210 --> 00:08:35,100
For you, it would be...

159
00:08:35,100 --> 00:08:36,450
...a magician, perhaps?

160
00:08:37,310 --> 00:08:39,310
-So simple-minded...
-So simple-minded...

161
00:08:41,990 --> 00:08:45,150
Come on, just write whatever,
it'll be okay.

162
00:08:45,280 --> 00:08:46,440
Dimple.

163
00:08:46,520 --> 00:08:49,220
Your future career won't be the same
as the one you wrote,

164
00:08:49,220 --> 00:08:50,930
no matter what you do.

165
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:54,300
I can't do that,
this is related to my future.

166
00:08:54,370 --> 00:08:57,850
You just can't ever lie, do you?

167
00:08:59,170 --> 00:09:01,240
What about your future prospects, Dimple?

168
00:09:01,240 --> 00:09:03,840
You're asking about
future prospects to a ghost?

169
00:09:03,840 --> 00:09:06,090
You're just naturally brutal, you know?

170
00:09:06,160 --> 00:09:07,530
Right.

171
00:09:07,800 --> 00:09:09,030
Sorry...

172
00:09:09,340 --> 00:09:11,080
Wait a sec...

173
00:09:11,610 --> 00:09:14,820
Wasn't there something I wanted to do...?

174
00:09:16,040 --> 00:09:19,240
That's right!
I forgot about it all this time!

175
00:09:19,880 --> 00:09:21,990
(Body Improvement Club)
Future aspirations, huh?

176
00:09:22,080 --> 00:09:24,190
My family runs a farm.

177
00:09:24,190 --> 00:09:28,040
After I finish high school,
I might have to succeed them.

178
00:09:28,460 --> 00:09:31,440
I'll just prioritize entering
high school for now.

179
00:09:31,440 --> 00:09:33,670
I got a recommendation to be an athlete.

180
00:09:33,760 --> 00:09:36,800
I'll look for a job
where I can train my muscles.

181
00:09:37,310 --> 00:09:42,320
My parents wants me to be a civil servant,
but my grades aren't that good...

182
00:09:42,420 --> 00:09:46,020
I like animals, so I decided that
I would be a veterinarian.

183
00:09:46,300 --> 00:09:49,440
You said you want to be a manga artist,
didn't you, Onigawara?

184
00:09:49,440 --> 00:09:52,520
Goddammit, Gouda!
How could you tell them?!

185
00:09:52,700 --> 00:09:54,858
-You said that you want to study

186
00:09:54,860 --> 00:09:56,068
-Hey! You don't have to say it out loud!
-You said that you want to study

187
00:09:56,070 --> 00:09:58,460
-Hey! You don't have to say it out loud!
-to enter a co-ed high school with a manga club.

188
00:09:58,760 --> 00:10:03,450
Everyone pretty much has decided
what they want in their future...

189
00:10:05,920 --> 00:10:09,640
Well, I have an thinking
about it all this time,

190
00:10:09,710 --> 00:10:13,170
but looking at your expression,
there's no more doubt.

191
00:10:13,340 --> 00:10:15,780
Mezato. What are you talking about?

192
00:10:15,840 --> 00:10:17,760
About the recent terrorist attack.

193
00:10:17,840 --> 00:10:22,260
While the world only thinks of it as vandalism
in the middle of a natural disaster,

194
00:10:22,350 --> 00:10:26,800
I'm sure that it's actually a fight
to decide the very fate of the world.

195
00:10:26,960 --> 00:10:30,140
In that fight, you managed
to defeat the evil organization,

196
00:10:30,400 --> 00:10:32,650
but you also lost something important.

197
00:10:33,120 --> 00:10:34,660
Isn't that right?

198
00:10:34,660 --> 00:10:37,130
No, I'm just thinking about
my future aspirations.

199
00:10:37,240 --> 00:10:40,400
No way! Just look at that!

200
00:10:40,510 --> 00:10:44,350
I'm totally sure that
you're related to that thing!

201
00:10:44,470 --> 00:10:47,120
Some even started calling it
the Divine Tree.

202
00:10:47,120 --> 00:10:49,290
People are starting to worship it.

203
00:10:49,430 --> 00:10:53,520
You should come out and tell everyone
that you're the creator of the Divine Tree.

204
00:10:53,680 --> 00:10:56,630
Is this related to that thing
you mentioned before?

205
00:10:56,730 --> 00:10:58,430
The Psycho Helmet Cult!

206
00:10:58,430 --> 00:11:00,590
Do you want to correlate
the two of them?

207
00:11:00,590 --> 00:11:04,470
(Psycho Helmet Cult)
Exactly! You catch pretty quick for once!

208
00:11:04,540 --> 00:11:08,200
You truly are amazing, Mob.

209
00:11:08,320 --> 00:11:12,060
I can't believe someone as mystical
as you is actually my classmate.

210
00:11:12,060 --> 00:11:14,200
Looking back at my entire life,

211
00:11:14,200 --> 00:11:17,390
you might be the biggest thing
that ever happened.

212
00:11:17,630 --> 00:11:20,030
Mezato, have you decided what
you'll become in the future?

213
00:11:20,080 --> 00:11:22,320
Huh? What's with this
all of the sudden?

214
00:11:22,650 --> 00:11:25,910
I'll probably be a cameraman.

215
00:11:25,990 --> 00:11:28,950
That, or a journalist.

216
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:36,540
I'm sure you'll find a lot more
exciting things in your future.

217
00:11:36,750 --> 00:11:39,630
Uh, I doubt there are many things
that can rival that.

218
00:11:39,720 --> 00:11:43,350
I'm not talking about some grand speech
or something physically big.

219
00:11:43,440 --> 00:11:44,940
Then, like what?

220
00:11:45,030 --> 00:11:48,880
For me, it's like when I joined
the Body Improvement Club.

221
00:11:48,960 --> 00:11:51,250
What's so big about that?

222
00:11:51,340 --> 00:11:54,070
It's not that different
from what you said.

223
00:11:54,200 --> 00:11:56,640
After all, that thing is just broccoli.

224
00:11:56,720 --> 00:11:59,070
I see, it's just broccoli...

225
00:11:59,070 --> 00:12:01,980
Yeah, right!
As if I'll agree to that!

226
00:12:02,060 --> 00:12:04,980
Then what about you,
what will you do in the future?

227
00:12:05,110 --> 00:12:08,540
The thing is, I couldn't think of any.

228
00:12:09,900 --> 00:12:13,930
After all that talk, I'm glad
you still have zero persuasiveness.

229
00:12:14,010 --> 00:12:17,290
Here I thought you got enlightened
or something after being too unpopular.

230
00:12:26,540 --> 00:12:32,760
There's no mistaking it,
I'm possessed by an evil spirit.

231
00:12:32,890 --> 00:12:36,900
I have contacted
many psychics before this,

232
00:12:36,970 --> 00:12:41,240
but not a single one of them
can exorcise the evil spirit.

233
00:12:41,360 --> 00:12:43,950
Uh... I see...

234
00:12:44,600 --> 00:12:48,680
I myself believe
"They" are definitely here.

235
00:12:48,760 --> 00:12:52,390
I knew it!
Hiring you was the right call!

236
00:12:52,460 --> 00:12:55,620
"They" are so scary!
The cockroaches!

237
00:12:59,980 --> 00:13:05,460
By the way, what are the exact specifics
that made you think that way?

238
00:13:08,490 --> 00:13:13,000
For starters, my shoulders feel heavy,
and I've been having sleep paralysis.

239
00:13:13,090 --> 00:13:17,750
There were also times when I developed
cavities even though I brushed my teeth.

240
00:13:17,980 --> 00:13:22,060
Maybe I also got fired from my
part-time job thanks to that evil spirit.

241
00:13:22,060 --> 00:13:26,990
A female co-worker kept saying that
I touched her butt even though I didn't.

242
00:13:27,170 --> 00:13:31,360
I just grazed them with the back
of my hand. It's an accident, really.

243
00:13:32,190 --> 00:13:35,960
Even my lover ran away
because of the evil spirit.

244
00:13:37,710 --> 00:13:39,800
Oh, your lover...?

245
00:13:39,800 --> 00:13:43,370
Yes. She was so young and nice.

246
00:13:43,480 --> 00:13:47,350
When I told her I'm running out of money,
her attitude took a 180.

247
00:13:47,470 --> 00:13:49,500
She's like an evil spirit herself.

248
00:13:49,610 --> 00:13:52,970
She once said that I'm her type,
what a bunch of lies.

249
00:13:53,710 --> 00:13:57,840
Oh, and I've been losing more
and more of my hair, too.

250
00:13:58,020 --> 00:14:01,550
It's as if someone is ripping them away.

251
00:14:01,660 --> 00:14:03,180
Is that so...

252
00:14:03,240 --> 00:14:05,250
By the way, what's with
all the trash?

253
00:14:05,320 --> 00:14:08,520
They're not trash!
They're my assets!

254
00:14:08,620 --> 00:14:11,320
A barrier of sorts.

255
00:14:11,470 --> 00:14:14,990
I can sleep soundly
if I'm surrounded by them.

256
00:14:15,190 --> 00:14:17,150
A barrier?

257
00:14:18,330 --> 00:14:20,000
What's this picture?

258
00:14:20,150 --> 00:14:22,000
Roach!

259
00:14:23,200 --> 00:14:27,740
An old picture of me,
back in my mischievous days.

260
00:14:29,470 --> 00:14:31,260
-He never changed...
-He never changed...

261
00:14:32,270 --> 00:14:35,690
You two, listen to his story.

262
00:14:36,800 --> 00:14:40,600
I'll go pick up a strong
exorcising tool...

263
00:14:42,840 --> 00:14:44,230
Okay.

264
00:14:48,690 --> 00:14:52,730
If nobody can exorcise my evil spirit,

265
00:14:52,730 --> 00:14:56,040
then maybe my life
is pretty much finished.

266
00:14:56,120 --> 00:15:01,670
Will I just keep on repeating
meaningless days until I die?

267
00:15:02,730 --> 00:15:07,630
My parents died when I'm in my 20's,
my relatives cut all connections to me.

268
00:15:07,770 --> 00:15:11,230
I don't have any connections,
so I can't get any jobs either.

269
00:15:11,530 --> 00:15:15,310
Maybe my life actually
is already finished.

270
00:15:15,450 --> 00:15:18,350
I know how you feel,
so very much.

271
00:15:18,480 --> 00:15:23,680
When I was a shut-in, I always thought
that it might be how my life will end.

272
00:15:23,870 --> 00:15:30,540
I'm also worried that I can't ever decide
on my future aspirations.

273
00:15:30,780 --> 00:15:35,680
I've lived for 50 years.
A long, long 50 years,

274
00:15:35,780 --> 00:15:40,510
yet the only thing I have left
is this house left by my parents.

275
00:15:40,680 --> 00:15:44,240
I never obtained anything.

276
00:15:44,410 --> 00:15:48,680
I just kept drifting around,
taking the easy choices.

277
00:15:48,850 --> 00:15:52,540
If only I seriously thought about
which path to pick back then...

278
00:15:52,720 --> 00:15:57,560
Your whole life can just end
the moment you make a single mistake...

279
00:15:58,030 --> 00:16:02,850
Enough already,
that's too much of a bother.

280
00:16:03,230 --> 00:16:06,110
There's no need to work so hard.

281
00:16:06,190 --> 00:16:08,410
It's 490 yen for one.

282
00:16:09,120 --> 00:16:11,740
It's 670 yen for two.

283
00:16:12,730 --> 00:16:15,030
It's 540 yen for one.

284
00:16:15,420 --> 00:16:18,000
Let's just do it tomorrow.

285
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:20,810
So tired, so lazy.

286
00:16:20,940 --> 00:16:24,140
Let's just sleep for today.

287
00:16:24,540 --> 00:16:26,490
Thankies.

288
00:16:27,540 --> 00:16:31,040
Evil spirits absolutely hate clean room.

289
00:16:31,040 --> 00:16:33,000
This should be...

290
00:16:33,120 --> 00:16:34,970
W-what's going on?

291
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:38,550
Oh, you got to be kidding me!

292
00:16:38,550 --> 00:16:40,310
That's from that trash house!

293
00:16:41,070 --> 00:16:43,850
You too, no need to work so hard.

294
00:16:46,510 --> 00:16:48,930
Are these the evil spirit's minions?!

295
00:16:49,500 --> 00:16:54,020
No need to work that hard.
Let's just sleep already.

296
00:16:55,990 --> 00:17:00,410
Double Hydrogenated Water Mist!

297
00:17:03,090 --> 00:17:05,960
A technique where Reigen uses
dissolved hydrogen gas

298
00:17:05,960 --> 00:17:10,450
to protect from evil spirit attacks.
One of his many special techniques.

299
00:17:11,520 --> 00:17:15,810
Of the evil spirit, by the evil spirit,
for the evil spirit...

300
00:17:17,130 --> 00:17:19,050
Hey, what the heck are you two doing?!

301
00:17:19,150 --> 00:17:21,720
Oh, Master. You're back?

302
00:17:21,850 --> 00:17:24,010
This isn't the time to say that!

303
00:17:24,100 --> 00:17:27,110
Look, an evil spirit showed up!

304
00:17:27,200 --> 00:17:28,950
Oh, you're right.

305
00:17:29,080 --> 00:17:31,820
So he was possessed
by something so big.

306
00:17:31,900 --> 00:17:36,600
No, I think that's actually
his vengeful spirit.

307
00:17:37,020 --> 00:17:38,630
Whatever.

308
00:17:38,700 --> 00:17:42,460
My power would be too strong and
may cause damage to the surroundings.

309
00:17:42,770 --> 00:17:45,000
Do it, you two.

310
00:17:45,510 --> 00:17:49,930
Of the evil spirit, by the evil spirit,
for the evil spirit...

311
00:17:50,080 --> 00:17:52,080
Of the evil spirit...

312
00:18:11,930 --> 00:18:13,350
Oh...

313
00:18:13,600 --> 00:18:16,800
Was this room this spacious again?

314
00:18:20,930 --> 00:18:23,640
Thank you so very much.

315
00:18:23,640 --> 00:18:28,330
Thanks to you, I think I can think
positively about life from now on.

316
00:18:28,460 --> 00:18:30,910
I'm glad to hear that, but...

317
00:18:31,050 --> 00:18:34,760
Your roof got, uh, blown up, so...

318
00:18:34,860 --> 00:18:40,430
My parents have it covered
with insurance, so it'll be okay.

319
00:18:42,010 --> 00:18:45,070
Yes, you can always
rely on insurance.

320
00:18:45,230 --> 00:18:46,700
Speaking of which,

321
00:18:46,830 --> 00:18:48,800
think of this as insurance, too.

322
00:19:07,060 --> 00:19:10,220
What's wrong, Serizawa?
Are you feeling sick?

323
00:19:10,420 --> 00:19:12,460
I just can't ignore what he said...

324
00:19:13,150 --> 00:19:14,900
I'm the same as him.

325
00:19:14,900 --> 00:19:18,970
I lived for 30 years,
and I don't have anything.

326
00:19:19,200 --> 00:19:22,930
You're not going to make it if you always
get affected by the customers.

327
00:19:23,050 --> 00:19:25,450
Your life isn't over just yet.

328
00:19:26,640 --> 00:19:31,490
If anything, you're lucky you noticed early
that you've done things you regretted.

329
00:19:31,660 --> 00:19:33,180
Right, Mob?

330
00:19:33,280 --> 00:19:36,460
I couldn't ignore what he said, either.

331
00:19:36,540 --> 00:19:37,840
You too?!

332
00:19:37,900 --> 00:19:41,870
I just haven't made any
huge mistakes yet,

333
00:19:41,950 --> 00:19:44,850
but that day may actually come.

334
00:19:44,960 --> 00:19:49,410
Just thinking about it makes me
too scared to pick any path.

335
00:19:49,990 --> 00:19:53,250
You were thinking about
something like that?

336
00:19:53,400 --> 00:19:57,340
Right, it's around the time
when he has to fill a future aspiration.

337
00:19:58,040 --> 00:20:00,760
I think you will be all right, Serizawa.

338
00:20:01,210 --> 00:20:04,870
You get to talk to many people
by working there,

339
00:20:04,870 --> 00:20:06,680
and you get to learn from it.

340
00:20:07,850 --> 00:20:10,230
But for me...

341
00:20:11,480 --> 00:20:14,230
(Progress until Mob explodes: 18%)

342
00:20:15,780 --> 00:20:19,190
So you're focusing on getting
to a high school for now, huh?

343
00:20:19,440 --> 00:20:22,780
In the end, I still can't
come up with anything.

344
00:20:22,970 --> 00:20:24,630
If you aim for a public school,

345
00:20:24,630 --> 00:20:27,370
you have to improve your math
and geography grades.

346
00:20:27,450 --> 00:20:30,190
You have to do better
on the next exams, Kageyama.

347
00:20:31,040 --> 00:20:32,480
O-okay.

348
00:20:32,480 --> 00:20:33,950
Is that it?

349
00:20:34,140 --> 00:20:37,700
That said, having a clear goal
in the future

350
00:20:37,700 --> 00:20:39,850
would help you plan your life better.

351
00:20:40,040 --> 00:20:41,790
You don't have to hurry,

352
00:20:41,790 --> 00:20:44,030
but it might be a problem
if you can't find one

353
00:20:44,030 --> 00:20:46,120
before you become an adult.

354
00:20:46,350 --> 00:20:51,640
Truth is, I only recently figured out that
I wanted to travel to many places alone.

355
00:20:51,770 --> 00:20:55,280
Things would've gone much easier
had I thought of it when I was younger.

356
00:20:55,430 --> 00:20:58,940
Then again, seeing how you did
on the marathon,

357
00:20:58,940 --> 00:21:00,470
I think you'll be just all right.

358
00:21:01,160 --> 00:21:02,510
Teacher...

359
00:21:02,920 --> 00:21:06,060
Becoming a traveler actually
sounds pretty nice.

360
00:21:06,140 --> 00:21:10,690
I'm actually quite worried about
how easily influenced you are...

361
00:21:11,160 --> 00:21:12,920
(Spirits and Such Consultation Office)

362
00:21:12,980 --> 00:21:15,120
I've been thinking about this
for quite a bit,

363
00:21:15,840 --> 00:21:20,670
but I think my future career
won't be here in this office.

364
00:21:22,420 --> 00:21:23,950
I see.

365
00:21:24,150 --> 00:21:29,120
This place is comfortable,
and I can discuss anything with you.

366
00:21:29,230 --> 00:21:31,250
But if I take that for granted...

367
00:21:31,390 --> 00:21:35,810
I won't grow anything
other than my physical age.

368
00:21:36,420 --> 00:21:38,460
I'm sorry, Master Reigen.

369
00:21:38,580 --> 00:21:42,400
I can't fulfill my promise
to keep working here in the future.

370
00:21:46,160 --> 00:21:49,920
Mob, that was obviously just a joke.

371
00:21:51,460 --> 00:21:55,030
You will find many things
you want to do from now on.

372
00:21:55,210 --> 00:21:59,630
You asked about why I opened
this consultation office, didn't you?

373
00:21:59,750 --> 00:22:01,530
Oh, yes.

374
00:22:01,710 --> 00:22:05,790
I gave you an answer back then,
but the truth is...

375
00:22:06,060 --> 00:22:11,390
I got bored in the company I worked in,
and made this office on a whim.

376
00:22:12,330 --> 00:22:16,590
Well, I got bored again in around a year
and was thinking of quitting.

377
00:22:16,880 --> 00:22:18,810
It was exactly then when...

378
00:22:20,460 --> 00:22:25,240
Well, this and that happened,
and it became what it is.

379
00:22:25,690 --> 00:22:28,650
It might have started on a whim,

380
00:22:28,650 --> 00:22:32,740
but it's not a lie that it has become
something I wanted to do.

381
00:22:32,880 --> 00:22:38,280
Anyway, the things you want to do
doesn't have to be a job.

382
00:22:38,380 --> 00:22:42,110
Just live the way you want it to be.

383
00:22:44,010 --> 00:22:46,040
Master Reigen...

384
00:22:46,220 --> 00:22:47,590
Got it!

385
00:22:51,910 --> 00:22:54,020
Thank you very much.

386
00:23:00,090 --> 00:23:03,670
Wait, we're still on working hours here...

387
00:23:03,900 --> 00:23:04,428
(001: The Future ~Career Aspirations~)

388
00:23:04,430 --> 00:23:06,830
Is he coming back?
(001: The Future ~Career Aspirations~)

389
00:23:06,831 --> 00:23:08,429
(001: The Future ~Career Aspirations~)

390
00:23:20,630 --> 00:23:22,450
Seems like the time has come.

391
00:23:22,560 --> 00:23:24,810
The time for my era.

392
00:23:26,220 --> 00:23:29,010
Those that squirm in the darkness
have started to make a move.

393
00:23:29,010 --> 00:23:31,790
Can the cycle of sadness be severed?

394
00:23:31,920 --> 00:23:34,160
Next on episode two of
Mob Psycho 100 III,

395
00:23:34,160 --> 00:23:37,390
"Yokai Hunter Haruaki Amakusa appears!
~The Threat of Hundred Demons! ~"

396
00:23:37,390 --> 00:23:39,900
Watching III in real-time
is also a wise decision.
